  "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={e}^{g},\\,g=\\operatorname{tanh}⁡s,\\,s={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}s}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}={e}^{g},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}s}={sech}^{2}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the three results together and substituting for $g$ and $s$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{g}\\cdot {sech}^{2}⁡s\\cdot 2x \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{2}}\\cdot {sech}^{2}⁡{x}^{2}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2x{e}^{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{sech}^{2}⁡{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
